<title>FRANCE: Eurotunnel sees fire report in three wks.</title>
<headline>Eurotunnel sees fire report in three wks.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eurotunnel SA Plc expects a report by the investigating magistrate on the causes of a November 18 fire in the cross-channel tunnel in two to three weeks, Operations Director Georges Christian Chazot said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not yet have the conclusions of the judge. We should have an answer in two to three weeks,&quot; Chazot told a news conference.  </p>
<p>The blaze in the tunnel connecting Britain and France started on a freight wagon, caused 200 million pounds of damage and a number of truck drivers on the train were taken to hospital.</p>
<p>The fire also forced the interruption of cross channel freight service through the tunnel from the date of the fire until it resumed on May 28.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
